          "entradaId": "freeman-470",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Mortars, for cracking grain by pounding with a pestle, are often used in the East. They are made of metal, earthenware, wood, or stone, the last being the most common material. The pestle is usually about five feet long. Sometimes two pestles are used at the same time for one mor…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-470",
          "sourceHash": "fe9dc80c5ef5866fb6c5b45d05e1e79325fc80ba90fa614351f2c248fb3ac369",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-ed259b111360bfa1": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-469",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See also Proverbs 19:13. Reference is undoubtedly made here to the frequent leaks to which the flat roofs of Eastern houses are subject. Having merely a covering of earth, rolled smooth and hard (see note on Psa. 129:6 #452), a heavy rain will soon succeed in finding its way thro…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-469",
          "sourceHash": "b88b55bb456d8408e449b6eede02b756fa89858068efc8cb17625cb665d51b0f",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      }
    },
